      "body": "Dr Reddys Laboratories Ltd. announced the launch of its injectable semaglutide under the brand name Obeda, marking an important step in expanding access to advanced GLP 1 receptor agonist based therapy for the management of type 2 diabetes in India. Dr Reddys has been the first Indian company to receive Drugs Controller General of India (DCGI) approval for generic semaglutide. This launch underscores the company's Day 1 entry into the segment upon patent expiry, demonstrating its readiness to serve unmet patient needs in India. India faces one of the world's largest diabetes burdens, with over 101 million adults living with the condition, according to the ICMR INDIAB study. The study estimates diabetes prevalence at 11.4%, with nearly four in ten adults experiencing abdominal obesity. An a",
